# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-11, pick P25). L §4.4: a computed value "carries the names it was computed from, as a
# window does its own, and a hole made of either carries them too"; L §8.2 `unknown day:` names each unknown day a
# hole of the result carries. A value computed from a window that a print needs as one value is the hole `not
# precise enough for a print`, made where the answer is printed: its unknown days are named like any hole's, each
# once, sorted with the rest (q1, q2: dx is computed from w and v; q3 beside a window value). A window value that
# prints as a window is no hole and names none (q4).
=== m.tally
model ph
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input w: date
input v: date
input d2: date

def dx: int = age(w, d2) + age(v, d2)

version r
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2000-03-01, 2000-03-31) "s"
  v = window(1990-03-10, 1990-03-20) "s"
  d2 = 2026-03-15 "s"

ask q1: age(w, d2)
ask q2: dx
ask q3: age(w, d2), w
ask q4: w
=== expect
q1: ?"date within window(2000-03-01, 2000-03-31) not precise enough for a print" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-30
q2: ?"date within window(2000-03-01, 2000-03-31) not precise enough for a print" (w)
  unknown day: v
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-30
q3: (?"date within window(2000-03-01, 2000-03-31) not precise enough for a print" (w), window(2000-03-01, 2000-03-31))
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-30
q4: window(2000-03-01, 2000-03-31)
  cut 2026-06-30
